<title>GERMANY: W.German June adjusted jobless falls 1,000 M/M.</title>
<headline>W.German June adjusted jobless falls 1,000 M/M.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 June 97	 May 97	   June 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.923 mln     2.960 mln	2.666 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.041 mln     3.042 mln	2.768 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		-1,000	  +26,000	  +6,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		 9.5 pct	9.6 pct	  8.7 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	120,318	 129,129	  214,748</p>
<p> Vacancies		   307,342	 308,671	  304,665</p>
<p>Change in number in work Apr 97	  Mar 96</p>
<p>				  -2,000	 +34,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
